---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
const lastUpdated = "July 31, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Editorial Policy — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={`${siteConfig.name}'s sourcing, fact-checking, and correction practices.`}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} is written and edited by a single author — see the{" "}
      <a href="/about/">About</a> page. This page explains how that content gets made
      and how mistakes get fixed.
    </p>

    <h2>How posts are researched and written</h2>
    <p>
      Posts are based on hands-on use of the tools, commands, and workflows
      described — code samples and configuration shown in a post are run and
      verified by the author before publishing, not copied from a single
      unverified source. Where a claim relies on official documentation, a
      changelog, or a specific tool's behavior, the post links directly to that
      source rather than asserting it without a reference.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} does not currently accept payment for coverage, and no post
      is written because a vendor requested it. See the{" "}
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate/Advertising Disclosure</a>{" "}
      page for the current, and any future, monetization status — if that ever changes,
      sponsored content will be labeled as such, both visibly and in the post's metadata,
      never blended into regular editorial content.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Software and tooling change quickly, and a post that was accurate on its
      publish date can go stale — a command gets deprecated, an API changes
      shape, a pricing tier moves. If you spot something outdated or incorrect,
      the fastest way to report it is via the{" "}
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page. Meaningful corrections are applied directly
      to the post; the site does not silently republish-and-hide a factual error.
    </p>

    <h2>AI-assisted writing</h2>
    <p>
      Some drafting, editing, and code-review work on {siteConfig.name} is done with
      AI coding assistants — this is disclosed here rather than hidden, since it's
      directly relevant to a site covering developer tools and AI productivity. Every
      post is still reviewed and tested by the human author before publishing; AI
      assistance changes how a post gets drafted, not whether it's been verified.
    </p>

    <p class="legal__disclaimer">
      This page is provided for transparency and is not a substitute for legal
      advice.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .legal__updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * -2);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
  }

  .legal__disclaimer {
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 8);
    padding-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
</style>
